      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VRC+ is enough already. In game currency will allow for some really asshole moves from creators, for example locking their avatars/worlds/world functions behind an in game paywall. We don't even know how the currency really works, how much of each transaction is VRChat taking for themselves. This is a prime example of corporate greed for financial growth. Corporate hate financial stagnation, it doesn't matter if you make the same amount each year, they require some % increase in revenue from previous year. That's how this works and they won't stop on this alone. If this works there's no telling on what they will do next. Hell they might attempt to implement crypto currency functions into their in game currency for all I know. I'm pretty sure everyone has heard about NeosVR crypto and NFT fiasco. Basically if this goes through VRChat will no longer be free to play anymore. Just imagine a world you go to every day suddenly is behind a paywall and you don't even know if you have to pay with each time you go into the world, or monthly, or however else they want you to pay.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
